      {
        "id": 113232,
        "name": "Oaktree",
        "username": "Oaktree",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/oaktree/{size}/2287_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-18T23:39:57.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Pydro\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/48/1844_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Pydro:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>It's based on the Bio-Eng Toxic Seaweed ruling. You can use Bio-Eng to destroy Toxic Seaweed and not take any damage, because Toxic Seaweed only triggers after the power resolves.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Which is sort of the opposite of the Informant ruling - where the Informant triggers a card play before the hero's card play can potentially destroy her.</p>\n<p>Though the latter mainly discussed card play as a trigger rather than power use as a trigger.</p>\n<p>-&nbsp; Given that I'd probably have been better off using Gung-ho on Finest Legacy to get a Galvanize maybe.</p>",
